{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nDiscovered while triaging breezy-hogged-mastiff, which owns `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/unclassified.args`. These 20 entries move to `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/locale-tests.args`, which this bug owns.\n\nThe test modules read Markdown, YAML and Terraform from the checkout with `read_text()` and no `encoding` (for example `tests/unit/test_rebar_debug_step7_class_review.py:29,34`, `test_code_review_ws2.py:176`, `test_gate_scratch_volume_aa40.py:163-234`). On Windows that decodes UTF-8 files as cp1252. Under `LC_ALL=en_US.ISO8859-1 PYTHONUTF8=0` on macOS all 20 fail even with the `src/rebar` encoding fix from dogtired-blank-fieldmouse applied; ruff `PLW1514` (preview) reports 228 sites in 108 test files.\n\nEvidence: Windows runs on throwaway branch `tmp/w05-remeasure` with origin/main `717c50f8b33` code plus a selection-only workflow change: run 44665461131 (the 242 `unclassified.args` entries; 48 passed, 194 failed or errored) and run 44681457334 (the 194, xdist, JUnit XML with full tracebacks). Both 2026-11-19 PST.\n\n## Root cause (established 2026-11-21 PST from the run 44681457334 tracebacks, read against origin/main `863abe7cd19`)\nThe 20 lines are 3 causes, not 1:\n1. **Locale decoding, 15 tests.** Test code reads a UTF-8 file with `Path.read_text()` / `open()` and no `encoding`, so Windows decodes it as cp1252: the em dashes and arrows in the prompt and doc files decode to other characters, so `test_measurement_provenance_criterion.py` (4) and `test_s4_prompt_cutover_edge.py` (1) compute different contract digests (for example `56d95dc4d520e255` vs pinned `c9ae05352df0062f` for `plan_review_F1.md`), section headings containing `—` are not found (`test_rebar_debug_step7_class_review.py:22` StopIteration, 7 errors), and the overlay catalog parse finds nothing (`test_code_review_recommend_overlays.py:158`, `test_code_review_surface_parity.py:114`, `test_code_review_ws2.py:177`).\n   The class is wider than these tests and includes product code. ruff `PLW1514` under-detects it: it flags a call only when it can infer a `pathlib.Path` receiver, so at `863abe7cd19` it reports 0 sites in `src` and `scripts` and 229 in `tests`. The class, as the guard defines it (`_is_locale_text_io`, `tests/unit/test_windows_text_encoding.py:180`): `read_text()` and `write_text(x)` with no `encoding`; text-mode builtin `open` and `io.open`; text-mode `os.fdopen`; text-mode `Path.open(mode)` with a literal mode; and text-mode `tempfile.NamedTemporaryFile`/`TemporaryFile`/`SpooledTemporaryFile` (`:161,196`); a non-literal mode or `**kwargs` is not judged. At `863abe7cd19` that finds **2264 calls: 16 in `src/rebar` (13 files), 15 in `scripts` (7 files), 2233 in `tests` (542 files)**. The `src` sites are product defects on Windows: for example `src/rebar/reconciler/load_phase.py:196,208` and `src/rebar/reconciler/applier.py:545,642` read reconciler snapshots and state as cp1252, `src/rebar/reconciler/apply_planning.py` writes through a text-mode `os.fdopen`, `src/rebar/_snapshot/repo_snapshot.py:166` reads the caveats sidecar, `src/rebar/graph/_unblock.py:44` a tombstone, `src/rebar/_snapshot/cache.py:115` and `janitor.py:279` cache counters. The earlier encoding fix (535e09284d3) relied on PLW1514 and so missed them. Calls on receivers the scan cannot type statically and other wrapper libraries are outside the guard; it is a floor, not a proof of absence.\n2. **Path separator, 3 tests** in `test_gate_scratch_volume_aa40.py`: `str(Path(\"/var/lib/rebar/gate-scratch\"))` is `\\var\\lib\\rebar\\gate-scratch` on Windows (`:274`, and the parent-bind checks at `:267`, `:288`). The product compares `Path` objects (`src/rebar/llm/gate_admission.py:82,120`), which is correct on Windows; the tests compare native strings with a POSIX container path.\n3. **POSIX shell recipe, 2 tests** in `test_makefile_worktree.py` (`test_successful_provisioning_still_succeeds`, `test_missing_gerrit_warns_but_still_creates_the_worktree`): the subject is the Makefile's worktree recipe run under `/bin/sh` with sh stubs, the same class as that module's other 6 tests in transhuman-wounded-pangolin.\n\n## Approach\n- Fix the class in product, scripts and tests: add `encoding=\"utf-8\"` to every site the AST scan reports (the 16 `src/rebar` sites, the 15 `scripts` sites, and the 2233 `tests` sites). Every file these sites read or write is rebar's own UTF-8 data (JSON state, Markdown, YAML, fixtures the test writes); none is meant to use the host locale, and `encoding=\"locale\"` / `cp1252` appear only where a test names them deliberately, which the scan leaves alone because an encoding is already given. The edit is applied by a deterministic codemod driven by the same AST scan (kept in session scratch, not committed), so it can be re-run unchanged after a rebase.\n- Keep it fixed: add `test_no_text_io_uses_the_locale_codec` to `tests/unit/test_windows_text_encoding.py`, the module that already guards `src/rebar` subprocess calls with an AST scan (`_locale_decoded_text_calls`, `test_no_src_call_decodes_child_output_with_the_locale_codec`). It scans `src/rebar`, `scripts`, `tests` and `hatch_build.py` with the rule defined in Root cause (`_is_locale_text_io`) and asserts no offenders, so a new locale-default call of those shapes fails on Linux CI before it reaches the Windows sweep. It is a plain pytest test, not a ruff config change, because PLW1514 cannot see the untyped receivers. No new config key, env var, flag or dependency.\n- Compare the 3 container paths as POSIX (`PurePosixPath`, `Path.as_posix()`).\n- Mark the 2 Makefile-recipe tests with the module's `_POSIX_SHELL_SUBJECT` skip (added by transhuman-wounded-pangolin's change, which lands first); their lines stay in `locale-tests.args`, recorded here as intentionally unsupported on Windows (subject is a POSIX shell recipe).\n- Sequencing: this change is rebased on transhuman-wounded-pangolin and foldable-gaseous-owl after they merge (they edit some of the same test files); the codemod is re-run on the rebased tree.\n\n## Scope\nProduct: the 13 `src/rebar` files and 7 `scripts` files listed by the scan (named in Root cause; full list recorded on the ticket when pushed). Tests: the 542 test files the scan reports, `tests/unit/test_windows_text_encoding.py`, `tests/unit/test_gate_scratch_volume_aa40.py`, `tests/unit/test_makefile_worktree.py`, and `.github/windows-sweep-deselect/locale-tests.args`.\n\n## Testing\n- Reproduce before and after on macOS: run the 15 locale tests under `LC_ALL=en_US.ISO8859-1 PYTHONUTF8=0` (fail before, pass after).\n- The new guard test fails on the pre-fix tree (2264 offenders) and passes after; its scanner is unit-tested with flagged and unflagged snippets (`read_text()`, `read_text(encoding=\"utf-8\")`, `write_text(s)`, `open(p)`, `open(p, \"rb\")`, `open(p, mode)` with a non-literal mode is not flagged).\n- A `sweep (windows)` run of the exact tree on `tmp/w3-azurevase`; after merge, the scheduled main sweep.\n- `make verify` through the verify-slot queue.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] Every line removed from `locale-tests.args` names a test that passed in a `sweep (windows)` run on main after the fix (run id recorded in a comment).\n- [x] `locale-tests.args` is empty and deleted with its reference in `.github/workflows/test.yml`, or each remaining line names a test recorded on this ticket as intentionally unsupported on Windows with the reason.\n- [x] `test_no_text_io_uses_the_locale_codec` in `tests/unit/test_windows_text_encoding.py` passes in `make verify` on the pushed tree (log path recorded in a comment) and fails on origin/main `863abe7cd19` (offender count recorded in a comment)."}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1795358213183638001,"uuid":"c497d880-7ba2-4d3f-83a9-fec0e77731bc"}